Here's a simple SystemVerilog module for an LDPC (Low-Density Parity Check) encoder for FPGA implementation:

```verilog
module ldpc_encoder(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire data_in,
    output wire data_out,
    output wire parity_out
);

reg [7:0] data_reg;
reg [3:0] parity_reg;

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset)
begin
    if (reset)
    begin
        data_reg <= 8'b00000000;
        parity_reg <= 4'b0000;
    end else
    begin
        data_reg <= data_in;
        parity_reg <= parity_gen(data_reg);
    end
end

assign data_out = data_reg[7:0];
assign parity_out = parity_reg[3:0];

function [4:0] parity_gen(data);
    // Implementation of LDPC parity generation logic here
    // ...
endfunction : parity_gen

endmodule
```

This module includes a 8-bit input data register, a 4-bit output parity register, and a parity generation function. The parity generation function can be implemented using various LDPC codes, such as the (255, 223) code or the (255, 191) code.

Note that this is a simplified example and may not meet all the requirements for a production-level FPGA design. For a more robust implementation, you should consider adding error detection and correction mechanisms, as well as optimizing the parity generation logic for performance and resource usage.

