edge_image_y = conv2(double(gray_image), sobel_y, 'same');

% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);

% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```

In this code, we first apply a Gaussian filter using the `fspecial` function. The `[3 3]` argument specifies the size of the kernel (3x3), and the `0.5` argument specifies the standard deviation of the Gaussian distribution. This helps to reduce the noise in the image before applying the Sobel operator.

