}
```

In this modified code, we use a try-catch block to handle the InputMismatchException. If the user enters a non-numeric value, the exception will be caught, and the program will display an error message asking the user to enter a valid integer. The Scanner.nextLine() method is then used to consume the invalid input, so that the next call to Scanner.nextInt() will read the correct value.

With these changes, your program should now handle input mismatches gracefully and avoid crashing with an exception.

