```javascript
function mapLinearToSmooth(value) {
  const startSmoothness = 0.2;
  const endSmoothness = 0.2;
  const linearRangeStart = 0.5;
  const linearRangeEnd = 0.5;

  if (value <= linearRangeStart) {
    return value * startSmoothness;
  } else if (value >= linearRangeEnd) {
    return (value - linearRangeEnd) * endSmoothness;
  } else {
    return value;
  }
}
```

This function takes a value between 0 and 1 as input and returns a value between 0 and 1 that starts smoothly, has a linear range in the middle, and then stops smoothly again. The `startSmoothness` and `endSmoothness` parameters control the smoothness of the beginning and ending parts of the curve, respectively. The `linearRangeStart` and `linearRangeEnd` parameters define the range of values over which the function behaves linearly.

You can adjust the values of these parameters to customize the shape of the curve. For example, increasing the `startSmoothness` or `endSmoothness` parameters will make the beginning or ending parts of the curve more gradual, while decreasing them will make them steeper. Similarly, changing the values of `linearRangeStart` and `linearRangeEnd` will shift the location of the linear range within the overall range of values.

